Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bazlur_Rahman_Badal$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bazlur%20Rahman%20Badal.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Dancer$b$, $b$Jalpaiguri district$b$, $b$Rajshahi$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Faisal Abedin Deepan$b$, DATE '1972-07-12', DATE '2015-10-31', $b$Attacks by Islamist extremists in Bangladesh took place during a period of turbulence in Bangladesh between 2013 and 2016 when a number of secularist and atheist writers, bloggers, and publishers in Bangladesh; foreigners; homosexuals; and religious minorities such as Hindus, Buddhists, Christians and Ahmadis who were seen as having offended Islam and Muhammad were attacked in retaliation, with many killed by Muslim extremists. 

By 2 July 2016, a total of 48 people, including 20 foreign nationals, had been killed in such attacks. These attacks were largely blamed on extremist groups such as Ansarullah Bangla Team and Islamic State of Iraq and Syria. The Bangladeshi government was criticized for its response to the attacks, which included charging and jailing some of the secularist bloggers for allegedly defaming some religious groups; or hurting the religious sentiments of different religious groups; or urging the bloggers to flee overseas. This strategy was seen by some as pandering to hard line elements within Bangladesh's Muslim majority population. About 89% of the population in Bangladesh is Sunni Muslim. The government's eventual crackdown in June 2016 was also criticized for its heavy-handedness, as more than 11,000 people were arrested in a little more than a week (as of 18 June 2016).

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faisal_Abedin_Deepan$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Academic, Journalist$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Muhammad Khasru$b$, NULL, DATE '2019-02-19', $b$Muhammad Khasru (1946 – 19 February 2019) was a Bangladeshi journalist and activist who pioneered the film society movement in the country. He played an important role in establishing the Federation of Film Societies of Bangladesh in 1973 and Bangladesh Film Archive in 1978.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Khasru$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Journalist$b$, $b$Hooghly district$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Mohamed Shah Alam$b$, DATE '1962-07-01', DATE '1990-05-29', $b$Mohamed Shah Alam (1 July 1962 – 29 May 1990) was a Bangladeshi sprinter. He was born in Shahebnagar village located in Gangni upazila of Meherpur district in a family of seven brothers and three sisters. His father Kabir Hossain was a footballer but none of his siblings pursued any sport. According to a report published on sports magazine Krira Jagat in 1990, Shah Alam joined Bangladesh Army as a Sepahi in 1977 and started participating in inter-unit competitions where he gained instant success. In the 100-metres sprint event, he won gold twice in 1985 South Asian Games in Dhaka and in 1987 South Asian Games in Kolkata. Alam competed in the men's 200 metres at the 1988 Summer Olympics. He also competed in the 1990 Commonwealth Games.

Alam was killed in a motorcycle accident on the Kushtia highway near Pabna while returning from Kushtia.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohamed_Shah_Alam$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Athletics competitor, Athlete$b$, NULL, $b$Kushtia$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Mohamed Mahbub Alam$b$, DATE '1972-10-01', DATE '2010-12-04', $b$Mohamed Mahbub Alam (1 October 1972 – 4 December 2010) was a Bangladeshi sprinter. In men's 200 metres sprint, he won gold in the 1995 South Asian Games in Madras and silver in the 1999 South Asian Games in Kathmandu. He also earned the national record of 10.54 seconds in the 100 metres sprint which 1996 Bangladesh National Athletics Championship. He received 2013 Bangladesh National Sports Award in the athletics category.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohamed_Mahbub_Alam$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Athletics competitor, Athlete$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Abdul Karim$b$, NULL, DATE '2007-07-24', $b$Abdul Karim (c. 1928 – 24 July 2007) was a Bangladeshi historian. He served as the 5th vice-chancellor of the University of Chittagong. He was awarded Ekushey Padak in 1995 by the government of Bangladesh. He was best known for his works on medieval and early modern Bangladeshi and South Asian history.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdul_Karim_(historian)$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Academic, Historian, Writer$b$, $b$Banshkhali Upazila$b$, $b$Panchlaish Thana$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Zubaida Gulshan Ara$b$, NULL, DATE '2017-03-19', $b$Zubaida Gulshan Ara (c. 1943/44 is a Bangladeshi writer. She was the chairperson of Bangladesh Shishu Academy. She was awarded Ekushey Padak in 2005 by the Government of Bangladesh.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zubaida_Gulshan_Ara$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer$b$, NULL, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Farid Ali$b$, DATE '1945-04-07', DATE '2016-08-22', $b$Farid Ali (7 April 1945 – 22 August 2016) was a Bangladeshi actor.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farid_Ali_(actor)$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Television actor, Actor$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Ibrahim Khan$b$, NULL, DATE '1978-03-29', $b$Ibrahim Khan (often referred as Principal Ibrahim Khan; c. 1894 – 29 March 1978) was a Bangladeshi litterateur. He was awarded Ekushey Padak in 1977 by the Government of Bangladesh.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibrahim_Khan_(writer)$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Aminul Islam (artist)$b$, DATE '1931-11-07', DATE '2011-07-08', $b$Aminul Islam (7 November 1931 – 8 July 2011) was a Bangladeshi artist. He was a part of Bangladesh modern art movement in 1950s. He was awarded Ekushey Padak in 1981 and Independence Day Award in 1988 by the Government of Bangladesh.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aminul_Islam_(artist)$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mohammad%2C%20Aminul%2C%20Rashid%20and%20Qayyum.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Artist$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sayed Haider$b$, NULL, DATE '2020-07-15', $b$Sayed Haider (December 1925 – 15 July 2020) was a Bangladeshi physician and Language Movement activist. He along with Badrul Alam designed the first Shaheed Minar. It was then demolished by the Pakistani Army on 26 February 1952. For his contribution to the Language Movement he was awarded Ekushey Padak in 2016.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sayed_Haider$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Language activist, Physician$b$, $b$Pabna$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Hasan Hafizur Rahman$b$, NULL, DATE '1983-04-01', $b$Hasan Hafizur Rahman (Bengali: হাসান হাফিজুর রহমান; 1932–1983) became the editor of the daily Bengali newspaper Danik Bangla right after the Bangladesh Liberation War in 1971. He also worked for the government as a high official and edited an account of the independence struggle called The Liberation War of Bangladesh, which was published in sixteen volumes. He was the author of thirteen books including eight collections of poetry and Adhunik Kobi O Kobita (Modern Poets and Poetry), a book of critical essays.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasan_Hafizur_Rahman$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Hasan%20Hafizur%20Rahman%20in%201963.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Journalist, Editor, Professor, Writer$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Aroj Ali Matubbar$b$, DATE '1900-12-17', DATE '1985-03-15', $b$Aroj Ali Matubbar (Bengali: আরজ আলী মাতুব্বর; 17 December 1900 – 15 March 1985) was a self-taught Bangladeshi philosopher, humanist and rationalist. He is known for his critical perspectives on religion, superstition, and traditional beliefs, which he expressed in his writings.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aroj_Ali_Matubbar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Aroj%20Ali%20Matubbar.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Philosopher, Author$b$, $b$Barishal$b$, $b$Barishal$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Arunabh Sarkar$b$, DATE '1941-05-29', DATE '2014-12-18', $b$Arunabh Sarkar (Bengali: অরুণাভ সরকার; born 29 May 1941) is a Bangladeshi poet, columnist, literary editor, and freedom fighter. He was born in Tangail, Bangladesh. He received the 2009 Bangla Academy Literary Award for poetry. Arunabh also received the Tangail Sahitya Sangsad Poetry Award for 2007. He has published three collections of poems : Nagare Baul, Keu Kichhui Jane Na, and Narira Fere Na. Sarkar also edited the poetry magazine Eshika from 1969 to 1985 and has been a journalist for some 40 years. He died on 18 December 2014.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arunabh_Sarkar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Arun%20dada.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Poet, Writer$b$, $b$Tangail District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Abdul Jabbar$b$, DATE '1938-02-10', DATE '2017-08-30', $b$Mohammad Abdul Jabbar (10 February 1938 – 30 August 2017) was a Bangladeshi singer. He is most widely known for his song "Ore Nil Doriya".

Also "Tumi Ki Dekhechho Kobhu Jiboner Porajoy", "Salam Salam Hajar Salam" and "Joy Bangla, Banglar Joy" were three of his songs which made it to the top 20 all-time Bangla songs in a 2006 survey by the BBC Bangla. He was awarded the Ekushey Padak in 1980 and the Independence Day Award in 1996 by the government of Bangladesh.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdul_Jabbar_(singer)$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mohammed%20Abdul%20Jabbar%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Singer$b$, $b$Kushtia District$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$A. M. Harun-ar-Rashid$b$, DATE '1933-05-01', DATE '2021-10-09', $b$Abul Maqsud Harun-ar-Rashid (1 May 1933 – 9 October 2021) was a Bangladeshi physicist and professor of physics at the University of Dhaka. He was the nephew of actor and writer Shamsuddin Abul Kalam.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._M._Harun-ar-Rashid$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Professor%20Harun%20ar%20Rashid.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Author, Physicist$b$, $b$Barishal$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sarder Jayenuddin$b$, NULL, DATE '1986-12-22', $b$Sardar Jainuddin (Bengali: সরদার জৈনুদ্দিন; 1 March 1918 – 22 November 1986) was a Bangladeshi novelist. He was awarded the Bangla Academy Literary Award in 1967. In 1994, he was posthumously honoured with the Ekushey Padak.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarder_Jayenuddin$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sordar%20Jainuddin.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Pabna District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Mita Haque$b$, NULL, DATE '2021-04-11', $b$Mita Haque (6 September 1962 – 11 April 2021) was a Bangladeshi Rabindra Sangeet singer. She had 14 solo musical albums released from India and 10 musical albums released in Bangladesh. She was awarded Ekushey Padak by the government of Bangladesh in 2020 for her contributions to music.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mita_Haque$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mita%20haque%20cropped%20from%20the%20image%20of%20Sheikh%20Hasina%20presents%20Ekushey%20Padak%202020%2C%20Osmani%20Memorial%20Auditorium%2C%20Dhaka%2C%202020-02-20%20%28PID-0034166%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Singer$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Shahnaz Rahmatullah$b$, DATE '1952-01-02', DATE '2019-03-23', $b$Shahnaz Rahmatullah (née Begum; 2 January 1952 – 23 March 2019) was a Bangladeshi Bengali singer.

Her notable songs are Sohni Dharti Allah Rakhay, Prothom Bangladesh Amar Sesh Bangladesh, Ekbar Jete De Na Amar Chotto Sonar Gaye, Je Chilo Drishtir Shimanay and Ek Tara Tui Desher Kotha. She was the recipient of the Ekushey Padak in 1992 and Bangladesh National Film Award for Best Female Playback Singer for the film Chhutir Phande (1990).

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shahnaz_Rahmatullah$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Shahnaz%20Rahmatullah%20with%20her%20brother%20Zafar%20Iqbal.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Singer$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Baridhara$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Polan Sarkar$b$, DATE '1921-09-10', DATE '2019-03-01', $b$Polan Sarkar (10 September 1921 – 1 March 2019) was a Bangladeshi social activist. He received the Ekushey Padak for social service from the Government of Bangladesh in 2011. He started a social movement to distribute books for free. He is known as "Alor Ferrywala," the distributor of light.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polan_Sarkar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Polan%20Sarkar.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Social activist$b$, $b$Natore District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Rahman$b$, DATE '1937-02-27', DATE '2005-07-18', $b$Abdur Rahman (known as Rahman; 27 February 1937 – 18 July 2005) was a Pakistani-Bangladeshi actor and film director. He acted in Bengali, Urdu, and Pashto films in Dhaka, Karachi, and Lahore from 1958 until 1993.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rahman_(Bengali_actor)$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%E0%A6%85%E0%A6%AD%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BE%20%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%B9%E0%A6%AE%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A8.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Actor$b$, NULL, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Ferdousi Priyabhashini$b$, DATE '1947-02-19', DATE '2018-03-06', $b$Ferdousi Priyabhashini (19 February 1947 – 6 March 2018) was a Bangladeshi sculptor. She was the first one to publicly announce herself as Birangona, a term coined by Sheikh Mujibur Rahman for the rape victims of the Liberation War of Bangladesh in 1971. Government of Bangladesh awarded her Independence Day Award in 2010.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdousi_Priyabhashini$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ferdousi%20Priyabhashini%20%281%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Sculptor$b$, $b$Khulna District$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Anil Mukherjee$b$, DATE '1912-10-10', DATE '1982-02-07', $b$Anil Mukherjee (Bengali: অনিল মুখার্জি; 10 October 1912 – 7 February 1982) was a Bangladeshi communist politician and writer. He was one of the leading figures of the communist movement in the British Raj, Pakistan (East Pakistan), and Bangladesh. He actively participated in the Bangladesh Liberation War in 1971.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Mukherjee$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%E0%A6%85%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B2%20%E0%A6%AE%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%9C%E0%A6%BF.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Politician, Writer$b$, $b$Munshiganj District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Amjad Hossain$b$, DATE '1942-08-14', DATE '2018-12-14', $b$Amjad Hossain (14 August 1942 – 14 December 2018) was a Bangladeshi film director, actor, scriptwriter and lyricist. He won the Bangladesh National Film Award for Best Director twice, for the films Golapi Ekhon Traine (1978) and Bhat De (1984). He also won Bangla Academy Literary Award in 2004 and Ekushey Padak in 1992.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amjad_Hossain$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Amjad%20Hossain%20-%20Bangladesh%20Film%20Archive%2040th%20founding%20anniversary%20inauguration%20by%20Information%20Minister%20Hasanul%20Haq%20Inu%202018-05-17%20%28PID-0044201%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Film director, Screenwriter, Writer$b$, $b$Jamalpur Sadar Upazila$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sanaul Huq$b$, DATE '1924-05-23', DATE '1993-02-04', $b$Sanaul Huq (23 May 1924 – 4 February 1993) was a Bangladeshi poet, translator, and civil servant. He had served as the first ambassador of Bangladesh to Belgium and the European Union during 1973–1976.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanaul_Huq$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sanaul%20Huq%20Brussels%201973.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Translator, Writer$b$, NULL, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Akhtar Hossain$b$, DATE '1945-11-01', DATE '2026-09-24', $b$Akhtar Hossain (Bengali: আখতার হুসেন; 1 November 1945 – 24 September 2026) was a Bangladeshi children's literature writer. He was awarded the Bangla Academy Literary Award and the Agrani Bank Shishu Academy Children's Literature Award in 2012, for his contributions to children's literature.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akhtar_Hossain$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Akhtar%20Hossain%20%289%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Children's writer, Writer$b$, $b$Natore District$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$S. M. Mohsin$b$, DATE '1948-01-30', DATE '2021-04-18', $b$S. M. Mohsin (30 January 1948 – 18 April 2021) was a Bangladeshi stage and television actor. He became an honorary fellow of the Bangla Academy in 2018. In 2020, he was awarded Ekushey Padak by the Government of Bangladesh for his contribution to acting.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S._M._Mohsin$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/S.%20M.%20Mohsin%20cropped%20Prime%20Minister%20Sheikh%20Hasina%20awards%20Ekushey%20Padak%202020%20at%20Osmani%20Memorial%20Auditorium%20Dhaka%202020-02-20%20%28PID-0034165%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Television actor, Stage actor, Actor$b$, NULL, $b$Bangladesh Institute of Research and Rehabilitation for Diabetes, Endocrine and Metabolic Disorders$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Faruque Alam$b$, DATE '1940-03-01', DATE '2020-05-24', $b$Faruque Alam (1 March 1940 – 24 May 2020) was a Bangladeshi civil engineer, wood technologist and the chairman of Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Corporation (BIWTC). He was elected member of parliament from Shariatpur-3 constituency during 1986 Bangladeshi general election under Jatiya Party banner.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faruque_Alam$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Faruque%20Alam%20%283%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Civil engineer, Politician$b$, $b$Shariatpur District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sukumar Barua$b$, DATE '1938-01-05', DATE '2026-01-02', $b$Sukumar Barua (5 January 1938 – 2 January 2026) was a Bangladeshi poet. While working in various positions at the University of Dhaka, Barua wrote critically acclaimed children's rhymes and literature. His works were mostly humorous in nature, with some carrying a political edge. For his works, he was awarded the Ekushey Padak by the government of Bangladesh in 2017.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sukumar_Barua$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%E0%A6%B8%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%95%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%AE%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B0%20%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%A1%E0%A6%BC%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%BE.png?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Hena Das$b$, DATE '1924-02-12', DATE '2009-07-20', $b$Hena Das (Bengali: হেনা দাস ; 12 February 1924 – 20 July 2009) was a Bangladeshi women's right activist and leftist. She was involved in Nankar Movement in 1948 and Bangladesh Liberation War in 1971. In 2001 she was awarded Begum Rokeya Padak by the Government of Bangladesh for empowering women and raising women's issues.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hena_Das$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Hena%20Das.JPG?width=640$b$, $b$Women's rights activist$b$, $b$Sylhet$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Fazal Shahabuddin$b$, DATE '1936-02-04', DATE '2014-02-09', $b$Fazal Shahabuddin (4 February 1936 – 9 February 2014) was a Bangladeshi poet and journalist. He was awarded Bangla Academy Literary Award in 1973 and Ekushey Padak in 1988.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fazal_Shahabuddin$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Fazl-Shahabuddin-2010.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Poet, Writer$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Pannya Jota Mahathera$b$, DATE '1955-12-22', DATE '2020-04-13', $b$Ven. U Pannya Jota Mahathera (Burmese: ဦးပညာဇောတမဟာထေရ်, Bengali: উ পঞ্ঞা জোত মহাথের; 22 December 1955 – 13 April 2020), locally known as Guru Bhante, was a Bangladeshi Theravada monk. He was born in a Royal Bohmong family in Bandarban, East Pakistan. He served the government of Bangladesh as a judge and magistrate for about eight years prior to becoming a Buddhist monk.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pannya_Jota_Mahathera$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/U%20Pannya%20Jota%20Mahathera.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Bandarban District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Kamal Dasgupta$b$, DATE '1912-07-28', DATE '1974-07-20', $b$Kamal Dasgupta (later Kamal Uddin Ahmed) (28 July 1911 – 20 July 1974), was a Bangladeshi Bengali music director, lyricist, composer and folk artist active in Hindi and Bengali cinema especially in pre-partition British India. Rāga and thumri were the main elements of his music. An ardent lover of Nazrulgeeti (the music of Kazi Nazrul Islam, National Poet of Bangladesh), he was immensely successful professionally, and in the early forties, was anecdotally reputed to have paid 35,000 to 40,000 rupees as income tax. On the other hand, a true humanitarian, during the Great Bengal Famine, when ten lakh starving and dispossessed people descended upon Calcutta, he opened langarkhanas (mass kitchens) and nearly spent the vast majority of his fortune to feed the needy and destitute. While in Calcutta, he lived in Tollygunge with his family. 

He later married Feroza Begum, a noted Nazrul Sangeet singer. Their second and third sons Hamin Ahmed and Shafin Ahmed were the lead singers with Bangladeshi band Miles.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamal_Dasgupta$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Music%20composer%20Kamal%20Dasgupta.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Singer, Composer$b$, $b$Kalia Upazila$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Rashid Choudhury$b$, DATE '1932-04-01', DATE '1986-12-12', $b$Rashid Hossain Choudhury (1 April 1932 – 12 December 1986) was a Bangladeshi second generation artist, sculptor, writer and professor. He played a major part in the art movements and improvement in the art-related educational institutions of Bangladesh. He has received numerous awards and recognition for creative contribution and innovative influence. During the 1950s, he had been a significant pioneer in the modern art movement in Bangladesh.

Choudhury received education in fine arts in Madrid and Paris. As such, a western influence can be seen in his uniquely Bengali work. Beside Art Movements, he made particular contribution in fine arts education in Bangladesh, founding the Chittagong Art College.

His works can be seen displayed across the world, by both public and private institutions.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rashid_Choudhury$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Rashid%20Choudhury%20%281932%20%E2%80%93%201986%29%20cropped.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Painter$b$, $b$Faridpur District$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Nazim Uddin Mostan$b$, DATE '1948-09-11', DATE '2013-08-18', $b$Nazim Uddin Mostan (September 11, 1948 – August 18, 2013) was a Bangladeshi journalist. He was a former chief reporter of The Daily Ittefaq until 1998. He was awarded Ekushey Padak in 2003 by the Government of Bangladesh for his contribution to journalism.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nazim_Uddin_Mostan$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Nazim%20Uddin%20Mostan.JPG?width=640$b$, $b$Journalist$b$, $b$Chandpur District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Enam Ahmed Chowdhury$b$, DATE '1937-06-29', DATE '2025-02-03', $b$Enam Ahmed Chowdhury (29 June 1937 – 3 February 2025) was a Bangladeshi civil servant who was secretary and chairman of the Privatization Commission. He was a member of Awami League and Bangladesh Nationalist Party.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enam_Ahmed_Chowdhury$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Inam%20Ahmed%20Chowdhury%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Economist, Writer$b$, $b$Golapganj Upazila$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Azharul Haque$b$, DATE '1940-03-02', DATE '1971-11-16', $b$Azharul Haque (Born 2 March 1940) is a Bangladeshi physician-surgeon, who has gone missing during the Bangladesh War of Independence.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azharul_Haque$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Azharul%20Haque-1.JPG?width=640$b$, $b$Physician$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Syed Safiullah$b$, DATE '1945-12-25', DATE '2016-06-11', $b$Syed Safiullah (25 December 1945 – 11 June 2016) was a Bangladeshi academic of chemistry. He was a professor in the Faculty of Mathematical & Physical Sciences at Jahangirnagar University (JU), Bangladesh. He was widely recognized for his research and innovation of Shushama fertilizer and fish feed, Safi Filter, and Safi Fuel. Among other positions, he was the former professor of chemistry and founder chairperson of environmental sciences department and Institute of Life Science at Jahangirnagar University (JU). His areas of interest covered environmental, material, synthetic, and applied chemistry. Safiullah is known for his work on arsenic pollution investigations, organic matter characterizations and environmental chemistry.

Safiullah was a Fellow of TWAS, the World Academy of Sciences, as well as a Fellow of the Bangladesh Academy of Sciences. He was a fellow of the international union of pure and applied chemistry (IUPAC) and he was the first fellow of the Royal Society of Chemistry, UK from the Jahangirnagar University.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syed_Safiullah$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Syed%20Safiullah.png?width=640$b$, $b$Scientist$b$, $b$Bagerhat District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Mishuk Munier$b$, DATE '1959-09-24', DATE '2011-08-13', $b$Ashfaque Munier (September 24, 1959 – August 13, 2011; known as Mishuk Munier) was a Bangladeshi media specialist and broadcast journalist. He was known for his photography direction and for being the cofounder of the global news channel The Real News Network. He was one of three sons of Munier Chowdhury. Mishuk served as the chief executive officer and chief editor of satellite TV channel ATN News. He died in a road accident, along with Tareque Masud, on August 13, 2011. He was awarded Ekushey Padak for his contribution to journalism in 2012 by the Bangladeshi government.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mishuk_Munier$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mishuk%20Munier.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Journalist, Author$b$, NULL, $b$Manikganj District$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Mizan Rahman$b$, DATE '1932-09-16', DATE '2015-01-05', $b$Mizan Rahman (September 16, 1932 – January 5, 2015) was a Bangladeshi Canadian mathematician and writer. He specialized in fields of mathematics such as hypergeometric series and orthogonal polynomials. He also had interests encompassing literature, philosophy, scientific skepticism, freethinking and rationalism. He co-authored Basic Hypergeometric Series with George Gasper. This book is widely considered as the standard work of choice for that subject of study. He also published ten Bengali books.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mizan_Rahman$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mizan%20mama.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Mathematician, Writer$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, $b$Ottawa$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Abney Golam Samad$b$, DATE '1929-12-29', DATE '2021-08-15', $b$Abney Golam Samad (29 December 1929 – 15 August 2021) (Bengali: এবনে গোলাম সামাদ) was a Bangladeshi academic, scholar, writer, columnist and public intellectual. His writings and speeches contained deep analyses of national and international society, politics, culture and literature. He was also a professor in the Department of Botany at the University of Rajshahi.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abney_Golam_Samad$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Abney%20Golam%20Samad%20by%20porag.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Sociologist, Professor, Writer$b$, $b$Rajshahi$b$, $b$Rajshahi Medical College$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Lalit Mohan Nath$b$, DATE '1935-11-01', DATE '2016-07-02', $b$Lalit Mohan Nath (1 November 1935 – 2 July 2016) was a Bangladeshi nuclear physicist. He was a professor in the Department of Physics at the University of Dhaka.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lalit_Mohan_Nath$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Lalit%20Mohan%20Nath.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Physicist$b$, $b$Chittagong$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Golam Sarwar$b$, DATE '1943-04-01', DATE '2018-08-13', $b$Golam Sarwar (1 April 1943 – 13 August 2018) was a Bangladeshi journalist and writer. He is considered the "LightHouse of journalism" in Bangladesh. He served as the founding editor of Samakal and Jugantor. He was awarded the Ekushey Padak by the government of Bangladesh in 2014.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golam_Sarwar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Golam%20Sarwar.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Journalist$b$, $b$Barishal District$b$, $b$Singapore$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Shantisudha Ghosh$b$, DATE '1907-06-27', DATE '1992-05-07', $b$Shantisudha Ghosh (27 June 1907 – 7 May 1992) also written as Shanti Sudha Ghosh was an Indian politician, writer, teacher and communist thinker and an admirer of Aurobindo Ghosh. She was a sister of Debaprasad Ghosh. She was the Founder Principal of Hooghly Women's College.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shantisudha_Ghosh$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Shantisudha%20Ghosh.png?width=640$b$, $b$Politician, Writer, Teacher$b$, $b$Barishal$b$, $b$Kolkata$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Kalidas Karmakar$b$, DATE '1946-01-10', DATE '2019-10-18', $b$Kalidas Karmakar (10 January 1946 – 18 October 2019) was a Bangladeshi artist. He specialized in viscosity printing. He was awarded Shilpakala Padak (2016) and the Ekushey Padak (2018) by the government of Bangladesh for his contribution to fine arts.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalidas_Karmakar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kalidas%20Karmaker%202016.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Painter$b$, $b$Faridpur District$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Papia Sarwar$b$, DATE '1952-11-21', DATE '2024-12-12', $b$Papia Sarwar (née Rahman; 21 November 1952 – 11 December 2024) was a Bangladeshi singer. She was an exponent of Rabindra Sangeet, the songs written and composed by Rabindranath Tagore. She earned the Rabindra Award from the Bangla Academy in 2013, the Bangla Academy Fellowship in 2015, and the Ekushey Padak in 2021.

Sarwar's notable songs include "Nai Telephone Nai Re Peon Nai Re Telegram".

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papia_Sarwar$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dhaka%20Ekushey%20Padak%202021%20Award%20Ceremony%20Papiya%20Sarwar%2C%202021-02-20%20%28PID-0030873%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Singer$b$, $b$Barishal$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Kazi Morshed$b$, DATE '1950-04-24', DATE '2014-10-03', $b$Kazi Morshed (24 April 1950 – 3 October 2014) was a Bangladeshi film director. He won Bangladesh National Film Award for Best Director for his film Ghani (2006).

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazi_Morshed$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kazi%20Morshed1.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Film director, Screenwriter$b$, $b$Chittagong$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Zahidur Rahman Anjan$b$, NULL, DATE '2025-02-24', $b$Zahidur Rahman Anjan (1964 – 24 February 2025) was a Bangladeshi film director. He won a Bangladesh National Film Award for Best Director for his direction of the film Meghmallar (2014). He taught filmmaking and film criticism at the Department of Film and Media Studies, Stamford University Bangladesh.

Anjan died of liver disease on 24 February 2025, at the age of 60.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahidur_Rahman_Anjan$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Zahidur%20Rahman%20Anjan%20at%20IFFI-2015.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Film director, Screenwriter$b$, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Ataur Rahman$b$, DATE '1941-06-18', DATE '2026-05-12', $b$Ataur Rahman (18 June 1941 – 12 May 2026) was a Bangladeshi stage and television actor. He was awarded Ekushey Padak in 2001 and Independence Award in 2021 by the government of Bangladesh for his contribution to drama. Rahman was known by the sobriquet Monchosharothi.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ataur_Rahman_(actor)$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ataur%20Rahman%20%28actor%29%20Jagroto%20Star%20Award%20Ceremony%20Bangladesh%20Shilpakala%20Academy%20Dhaka%202022-06-03%20%28PID-0022863%29%20%28cropped%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Television actor, Actor$b$, $b$Noakhali District$b$, NULL);
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Musharraf Karim$b$, DATE '1946-01-09', DATE '2020-01-11', $b$Musharraf Karim (9 January 1946 – 11 January 2020) was a Bangladeshi writer and journalist. He was conferred with the Bangla Academy Literary Award in 2003 for his contribution to juvenile literature. He was a fellow of the Bangla Academy.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musharraf_Karim$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Musharraf%20Karim.JPG?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Mymensingh$b$, $b$Mymensingh$b$);
